<title>UK: GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>GOLF-WORLD RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mark O'Meara, winner of the Buick</p>
<p>Invational at the weekend, has narrowed the gap on third and</p>
<p>fourth-placed Colin Montgomerie and Ernie Els in the weekly</p>
<p>world rankings issued on Monday.</p>
<p>O'Meara is now just 0.11 of a point behind both men who are</p>
<p>on 8.95 points.</p>
<p>The top five places remain unchanged with Greg Norman</p>
<p>remaining clear at the top ahead of Tom Lehman.</p>
<p>Tiger Woods remains unchanged in 14th spot despite his</p>
<p>10-stroke victory in the Asian Honda Classic which is not an</p>
<p>official world ranking tournament.</p>
<p>Top 20 (U.S. unless stated):</p>
<p>  1. Greg Norman (Australia)     11.70 points average</p>
<p>  2. Tom Lehman			 9.82</p>
<p>3. Colin Montgomerie (Britain)  8.95</p>
<p>  4. Ernie Els (South Africa)     8.95</p>
<p>  5. Mark O'Meara		     8.84</p>
<p>  6. Nick Faldo (Britain)	   7.98</p>
<p>  7. Fred Couples		     7.77</p>
<p>  8. Masashi Ozaki (Japan)	  7.58</p>
<p>  9. Davis Love III		   6.85</p>
<p> 10. Corey Pavin			6.80</p>
<p> 11. Phil Mickelson		   6.45</p>
<p> 12. Nick Price (Zimbabwe)	  6.43</p>
<p> 13. Steve Stricker		   6.17</p>
<p> 14. Tiger Woods			5.72</p>
<p>15. Steve Elkington (Australia)  5.70</p>
<p> 16. Scott Hoch			 5.69</p>
<p> 17. David Duval			5.50</p>
<p> 18. Bernhard Langer (Germany)    5.49</p>
<p> 19. Steve Jones			5.37</p>
<p> 20. Tom Watson			 5.35</p>
</text>
